{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And I said to you at that time, saying.</b> What is לֵאמֹר? Moses said to them: I am not saying this on my own, but from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>I cannot bear you alone, etc.</b> Is it possible that Moses could not judge Israel? The man who brought them out of Egypt, and split the sea for them, and brought down the manna, and drove in the quail — he could not judge them? Rather, this is what he said to them: <b>YHWH your Elohim has multiplied you</b> — He has made you great and exalted you above your judges; He has taken the punishment from you and placed it upon the judges. And so said Solomon (1 Kings 3): ״For who is able to judge this great people of Yours?״ Is it possible that he concerning whom it is written (ibid. 5) ״He was wiser than all men״ says ״Who is able to judge?״ Rather, this is what Solomon said: The judges of this nation are not like the judges of other nations — for if [their judges] judge and kill and strike and strangle and pervert their judgment and rob, there is nothing in it; but I — if I wrongly imposed a monetary liability, I am held accountable for lives, as it is said (Proverbs 22) ״and He takes the soul of those who wrong them.״ (Sifrei; Sanhedrin 7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:24.942513324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}